Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: apply the vSafe0V VBUS fallback only as sink

0021 counts VBUS as present whenever the state machine says it is not at
vSafe0V, to ride through USB-PD voltage steps while sinking. It also applied
while sourcing and toggling, and set_cc() state (Rd) survived into
start_toggling(). After a sink session, a supply that was still discharging
read as present and no interrupt fires when it reaches vSafe0V, so TCPM never
saw vSafe0V and sat in SRC_ATTACH_WAIT (an unpowered USB-C HDMI adapter
never attached).

Track whether we present Rd and use the fallback only then; clear it when
toggling starts.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c	2026-11-13 20:33:26.416648931 +0100
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c	2026-11-13 20:34:01.336050472 +0100
@@ -177,6 +177,7 @@
 	struct mutex			vbus_lock;		/* VBUS state serialization */
 
 	int				cc;
+	bool				sinking;	/* Rd presented: VBUS may step */
 	bool				debouncing_cc;
 	struct delayed_work		cc_debounce_dwork;
 
@@ -296,8 +297,13 @@
 	 * detach and the contract is torn down during the voltage transition,
 	 * forever. The state machine status also tells whether VBUS sits at
 	 * vSafe0V; anything above that is a present supply.
+	 *
+	 * Only while we present Rd. As a source or while toggling, a supply
+	 * that is merely still discharging must read as absent: nothing
+	 * interrupts again when it reaches vSafe0V, so TCPM would wait in
+	 * SRC_ATTACH_WAIT for vSafe0V forever.
 	 */
-	if (!vbus) {
+	if (!vbus && READ_ONCE(pmic_typec_port->sinking)) {
 		ret = regmap_read(pmic_typec_port->regmap,
 				  pmic_typec_port->base + TYPEC_SM_STATUS_REG,
 				  &sm);
@@ -528,6 +534,7 @@
 	}
 
 	pmic_typec_port->cc = cc;
+	WRITE_ONCE(pmic_typec_port->sinking, cc == TYPEC_CC_RD);
 	qcom_pmic_set_cc_debounce(pmic_typec_port);
 	ret = 0;
 
@@ -624,6 +631,7 @@
 		misc, !!(misc & CC_ATTACHED), port_type, pmic_typec_port->cc, cc);
 
 	qcom_pmic_set_cc_debounce(pmic_typec_port);
+	WRITE_ONCE(pmic_typec_port->sinking, false);
 
 	/* force it to toggle at least once */
 	ret = regmap_write(pmic_typec_port->regmap,
